{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334452-orpheus-future","id":334452,"title":"Orpheus' future","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-08T12:56:31-08:00","id":334452,"title":"Orpheus' future","content":"So, with Orpheus included in Wr20, is there any chance at all that the game will get it's own Kickstarter down the line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T13:03:08-08:00","id":334463,"title":"","content":"That would be too far in the future for us to know at this point. For now, our plans for <i>Orpheus</i> are tied in with <i>Wraith 20</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:50:23-08:00","id":334701,"title":"","content":"A 20th anniversary edition of Orpheus wouldn't be until 2023, which is nine years off: way further than we currently plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:54:51-08:00","id":334703,"title":"","content":"I was sort of hoping the other games (Demon, Hunter, maybe Orpheus) might get 10th Anniversary Editions. I would hate to have to wait another ten years for a re-release of Demon: The Fallen, one of my favourite cWoD games of all time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T21:43:02-08:00","id":334827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EisenKreutzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334452-orpheus-future?p=334703#post334703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was sort of hoping the other games (Demon, Hunter, maybe Orpheus) might get 10th Anniversary Editions. I would hate to have to wait another ten years for a re-release of Demon: The Fallen, one of my favourite cWoD games of all time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd be ecstatic to see DtF get an Anniversary Edition anytime soon. Especially because the Halaku make for such good crossover stuff with WtO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T12:18:32-08:00","id":336203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EisenKreutzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334452-orpheus-future?p=334703#post334703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was sort of hoping the other games (Demon, Hunter, maybe Orpheus) might get 10th Anniversary Editions. I would hate to have to wait another ten years for a re-release of Demon: The Fallen, one of my favourite cWoD games of all time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter's 10th anniversary was 2009, Demon's 10th anniversary was 2012, and Orpheus' was 2013. If we were doing those, we'd be late (five years late in the case of Hunter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T12:23:52-08:00","id":336205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334452-orpheus-future?p=336203#post336203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunter's 10th anniversary was 2009, Demon's 10th anniversary was 2012, and Orpheus' was 2013. If we were doing those, we'd be late (five years late in the case of Hunter).</div> </div> </div> </div>All true, of course. Call it 15th then. :P Look, this is more wishful thinking than anything else. I'd hate to have to wait until 2019 or 2022 to see these two amazing games get new editions, but ultimately this decision rests with you guys. I know there are many, many fans of these games who would absolutely adore new editions in the vein of the 20th books and would happily throw their wallets at such a project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T14:46:58-08:00","id":336324,"title":"","content":"Give me Kindred of the East - Demon and Orpheus as a Deluxe edition it will all be golden <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think i will back Changeling 20th ed if they try to wait a good few months with it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Then it would have been only M20 i did not back. hunter i am not to fond of so I am unsure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1159-kjetilkverndokken","name":"kjetilkverndokken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1159_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T17:42:37-08:00","id":336516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EisenKreutzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334452-orpheus-future?p=336205#post336205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All true, of course. Call it 15th then. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Still missing the boat on <b>Hunter</b>, as OPP is going to have its hands full with Wr20 and C20 in 2015. As well, the 20th Anniversary Editions are starting to run late: Mage\u2019s 20th anniversary was in 2013, and it looks like the commemorative edition may not be out until 2015. Wr20 has just barely gotten its KS started before its 20th Anniversary ends; and I won\u2019t be surprised if C20\u2019s KS doesn\u2019t get started until early 2016. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look, this is more wishful thinking than anything else. I'd hate to have to wait until 2019 or 2022 to see these two amazing games get new editions, but ultimately this decision rests with you guys. I know there are many, many fans of these games who would absolutely adore new editions in the vein of the 20th books and would happily throw their wallets at such a project. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. That said, the \u201c20th Anniversary commemorative edition\u201d thing seems to be morphing. After C20, I\u2019d drop the \u201c20th Anniversary Edition\u201d schtick entirely and just go about the business of publishing Second Editions, something no game after <b>Changeling</b> got (Unless you count <b>Mummy: the Resurrection</b> as a third edition of <b>Mummy</b> \u2014 which I don\u2019t, due to the drastic changes that took place in the underlying premise). <br /> <br /> The other thing I\u2019d do with <b>Hunter</b>, <b>Mummy</b>, and <b>Demon</b> would be to recast them in a way where they <i>don\u2019t</i> include an impoicit assumption that the world is coming to an end. I\u2019d take my cue from the recent <b>Mage</b> Revised Convention Books: yes, something profound occurred in 1998 that transformed the world forever, releasing demons and hunters imbued with divine power onto the earth and transforming Osiris\u2019 children forever; but if the world is coming to an end, it sure is taking its time doing so \u2014 and these days, few people seriously think the end is coming any time soon. <br /> <br /> Heck, I\u2019d like to go one step further, and have each of these games include an Appendix dedicated to \u201chow to use this book in a game set before the rise of the ghost storm\u201d. <b>Demon</b> would take its cue from the <b>Devil\u2019s Due</b> Dark Ages supplement; <b>Hunter</b> would take <i>its</i> cue from <b>Dark Ages: Inquisitor</b> with the notion that a few \u201cloose cannons\u201d among the Messengers have always been around, granting power to select mortals they deem worthy of their gifts (i.e., <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s Creeds, Virtues, and Edges as a recasting of True Faith); and <b>Mummy</b> would show how the game can be recast in terms of the premise of the first two editions of <b>Mummy</b> (immortals caught in an eternal cycle of death and resurrection). For those interested in crossovers, that would open up additional avenues where the latter-day games could be made to fit in with the pre-Reckoning World of Darkness instead of requiring the older games to be set in the post-Reckoning era; for those <i>not</i> interested in crossovers, it would provide ways to play these games without the notion that these guys are the first of their kind.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As for <b>Orpheus</b>, the inclusion of the company (and presumably of many of its conceptual innovations) into the framework of Wr20 leads me to wonder if an <b>Orpheus 2e</b> would overlap too much with Wr20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-10-2014, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T16:33:39-08:00","id":337481,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'm hoping for some of Orpheus's improvements to make it into the main book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T07:04:50-08:00","id":370986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334452-orpheus-future?p=336516#post336516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: As for <b>Orpheus</b>, the inclusion of the company (and presumably of many of its conceptual innovations) into the framework of Wr20 leads me to wonder if an <b>Orpheus 2e</b> would overlap too much with Wr20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Orpheus' setting requires the complete annihilation of Wraith's, they're not likely to co-exist in a peaceable manner. Even the mere presence of an Orpheus Group starts to warp the setting of Wraith into something far different than the original portrayal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T07:24:09-08:00","id":371015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334452-orpheus-future?p=370986#post370986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Orpheus' setting requires the complete annihilation of Wraith's, they're not likely to co-exist in a peaceable manner. Even the mere presence of an Orpheus Group starts to warp the setting of Wraith into something far different than the original portrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes a lot of sense: your inability to interact with the Skinlands like one of the Quick, and that at best the people you knew generally consider you to either be in some sort of remote afterlife or wholly having ceased to exist, is a fairly critical part of Wraith. Meanwhile, Orpheus more or less confirms the existence of Post-Life Entities, and the world at large now <i>knows</i> that there's some sort of life--or at least continued state of being--after death. These two are, at best, difficult to reconcile.<br /> <br /> This also makes me wonder quite a bit about what the Orpheus section we're getting is going to look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:00:26-08:00","id":371042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334452-orpheus-future?p=371015#post371015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This also makes me wonder quite a bit about what the Orpheus section we're getting is going to look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well, you're not the one writing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's been a much larger challenge that I'd ever anticipated, but I think I'm striking a good balance between Wraith and Orpheus that doesn't compromise either game. Let's hope I've hit the mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:25:46-08:00","id":371060,"title":"","content":"I understand what you meant, Mockery, but following your logic the chapter about the Risen wouldn't make sense either, then.<br /> <br /> I think Orpheus can simply be used as another window to look through at the Underworld. Just to allow more experiences. It may be easier to 'digest' for players not used to WtO, or simply easier to handle if you do not wish to deal with the Passions and Shadowguiding. And like for the Risen, it can be useful if you want to play a crossover with Vampires for instance. That said, I wouldn't recommend a mix of projecters and Wraith among the PCs.<br /> <br /> For me it follows what had been started in the Mediums add-on: what do the Quicks know about the Underworld and how do they interract with it. True that Orpheus setting implied the (almost) complete annihilation of the Wraith's one, but WtO is no more contradictory to Orpheus than to Wraith20... I mean: unless Wraith20 is specifically set before the 'End of Empire', and therefore wished as a retro game set in the 90's, it will also imply some changes in the 'axioms' of the universe as we know it.<br /> <br /> Who knows? Maybe Orpheus has only access to restricted portions of the Shadowlands, or maybe they do not even have access at all to the Underworld: they could only project in alternate plane of existence, between the Skinland and the Shadowland... inside the Shroud!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}